{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-129550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y{[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡0]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =2-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129550" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdc9755692590715d69778410eed7c74fc2ff3ed1475976305ec45b51df123cc"} {"question" "q-129550" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129550" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129550" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the repeated integral\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}{[-\\frac{1}{x}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}(-\\frac{1}{2}-(-1))\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{1-{y}^{2}}}\\text{d}y & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y]_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdc9755692590715d69778410eed7c74fc2ff3ed1475976305ec45b51df123cc"} {"question" "q-73578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73578" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{12}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant. \n\nMaking a substitution $x+y=u,$ $\\text{d}x=\\text{d}u,$ we get.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{y}^{1+y}\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{[-\\frac{1}{u}]}_{y}^{1+y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(-\\frac{1}{y+1}+\\frac{1}{y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}[\\frac{1}{y}-\\frac{1}{y+1}]\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}[\\frac{1}{y}-\\frac{1}{y+1}]\\,\\text{d}y & =[\\operatorname{ln}⁡y-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y+1)]_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{y}{y+1}){|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129549" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdc9755692590715d69778410eed7c74fc2ff3ed1475976305ec45b51df123cc"} {"question" "q-129549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{2}{3})"] ["math" "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})+3"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129549" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{4}{3})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the repeated integral\n${\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}{\\int }_{1/3}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}(1+9{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}[{\\int }_{1/3}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{3}{{y}^{2}(1+9{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{1/3}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\frac{3}{(1+(3x)^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3x)]_{1/3}^{\\sqrt{3}/3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{3})-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1))\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{\\pi }{12{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{1/4}\\frac{\\pi }{12{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[-\\frac{\\pi }{12y}]}_{1/3}^{1/4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{12\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}}+\\frac{\\pi }{12\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73583" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdc9755692590715d69778410eed7c74fc2ff3ed1475976305ec45b51df123cc"} {"question" "q-73583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{\\pi }{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{3\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73583" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{\\pi }{12}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-37951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the repeated integral\n${\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-37951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}(1+{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\frac{1}{(1+{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}[\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x]_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3}-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡0)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{\\pi }{3{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}\\frac{\\pi }{3{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[-\\frac{\\pi }{3y}]}_{-2}^{-1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3\\cdot (-1)}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{3\\cdot (-2)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-37951" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdc9755692590715d69778410eed7c74fc2ff3ed1475976305ec45b51df123cc"} {"question" "q-37951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-37951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{\\pi }{3}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-37951" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\pi }{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72268" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72268" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,[\\operatorname{sin}⁡x]_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y(1-0)\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =-2[\\operatorname{cos}⁡y]_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-2\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =2-\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72268" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdc9755692590715d69778410eed7c74fc2ff3ed1475976305ec45b51df123cc"} {"question" "q-72268" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72268" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "2-\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72268" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2-\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}y{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}[{e}^{xy}]_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}({e}^{1\\cdot y}-{e}^{0\\cdot y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}({e}^{y}-1)\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}({e}^{y}-1)\\text{d}y & =[{e}^{y}-y]_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =({e}^{4}-4)-({e}^{0}-0)\\text{ } \\\\  & ={e}^{4}-4-1 \\\\  & ={e}^{4}-5\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72264" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdc9755692590715d69778410eed7c74fc2ff3ed1475976305ec45b51df123cc"} {"question" "q-72264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "e"] ["math" "e-1"] ["math" "{e}^{2}+2"] ["math" "{e}^{2}-2"] ["math" "{e}^{4}-5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72264" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{4}-5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}xy\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}xy\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y[{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y(\\frac{{1}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{y}{2}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72197" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdc9755692590715d69778410eed7c74fc2ff3ed1475976305ec45b51df123cc"} {"question" "q-72197" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72197" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72197" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:   \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{[{e}^{x+y}]}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({e}^{1+y}-{e}^{0+y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({e}^{1+y}-{e}^{y})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(e{e}^{y}-{e}^{y})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{y}(e-1)\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{y}(e-1)\\text{d}y & =(e-1)[{e}^{y}]_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(e-1)({e}^{2}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =(e-1)({e}^{2}-1) \\\\  & ={e}^{3}-{e}^{2}-e+1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdc9755692590715d69778410eed7c74fc2ff3ed1475976305ec45b51df123cc"} {"question" "q-72267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{e}^{3}+{e}^{2}+e+1"] ["math" "{e}^{3}+{e}^{2}-e-1"] ["math" "{e}^{3}-1"] ["math" "{e}^{3}-{e}^{2}+e-1"] ["math" "{e}^{3}-{e}^{2}-e+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{e}^{3}-{e}^{2}-e+1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73591" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral ${∬}_{D}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A,$ where \n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{e}^{2}\\le x\\le {e}^{4},\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt[3]{6}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73591" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:      \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}[{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}[{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡x]_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{4}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{2}{3}[{y}^{3}]_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}((\\sqrt[3]{6})^{3}-{0}^{3}) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73591" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdc9755692590715d69778410eed7c74fc2ff3ed1475976305ec45b51df123cc"} {"question" "q-73591" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73591" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\sqrt[3]{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73591" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\le y\\le 2}.$\n\n- ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n- ${∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice that:  \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $0$ to $\\sqrt{2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $-\\sqrt{3}$ to $2.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{2}}[{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{2}\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72175" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdc9755692590715d69778410eed7c74fc2ff3ed1475976305ec45b51df123cc"} {"question" "q-72175" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72175" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72175" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant. \n\nMaking a substitution $xy=u,$ $\\text{d}y=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}u,$ we get.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{x}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{e}^{u}]_{0}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}-1)\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}-1)\\,\\text{d}x & =[{e}^{x}-x]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(e-1)-(1-0) \\\\  & =e-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129645" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdc9755692590715d69778410eed7c74fc2ff3ed1475976305ec45b51df123cc"} {"question" "q-129645" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129645" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1-2e"] ["math" "2e"] ["math" "e+1"] ["math" "e-1"] ["math" "e-2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129645" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\le y\\le 1}.$\n\n- ${∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$\n- ${∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$\n- ${∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice that:\n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from $1$ to $2$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from $\\frac{1}{2}$ to $1.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{1}^{2}[{\\int }_{1/2}^{1}y\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72130" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdc9755692590715d69778410eed7c74fc2ff3ed1475976305ec45b51df123cc"} {"question" "q-72130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-72130" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{1}^{2}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}[{\\int }_{1}^{2}(x+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,{[xy+\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}[(2x+\\frac{8}{3})-(x+\\frac{1}{3})]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\frac{7}{3})\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(x+\\frac{7}{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{7x}{3}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{7}{3})-(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{7}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129644" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdc9755692590715d69778410eed7c74fc2ff3ed1475976305ec45b51df123cc"} {"question" "q-129644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{14}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-129644" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{14}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the repeated integral ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{3}^{x}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{{3}^{x}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}[{\\int }_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡y]_{{e}^{-1}}^{{e}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{3}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{-1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{3}^{x}(3+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{[\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4(\\frac{{3}^{1}-{3}^{0}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73601" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "fdc9755692590715d69778410eed7c74fc2ff3ed1475976305ec45b51df123cc"} {"question" "q-73601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "8\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "q-73601" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/state.json" "file_sha256" "5902b2c268a80df98c7e46ebe9bb6deaf8d8263e62215afcdfe5e8f60fcff68f"} {"question" "e-6097" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the repeated integral $\\displaystyle \\int_{2}^{4}  \\int_{0}^{2} \\dfrac{x^3}{y^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x  \\, \\textrm{d}y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/example-6097.json" "file_sha256" "21b0f5a4dfa11c65181d896915038cf4bb17ce4faa90bdbcd6fa935b9c00e834"} {"question" "e-6097" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{4}}{4})\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{4}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4{[-\\frac{1}{y}]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =4(-\\frac{1}{4}-(-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/example-6097.json" "file_sha256" "21b0f5a4dfa11c65181d896915038cf4bb17ce4faa90bdbcd6fa935b9c00e834"} {"question" "e-6098" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} \\dfrac y{x^2} \\, \\textrm d A$, where \n$D=\\left\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\:2 \\leq x \\leq 4,\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 3\\right\\}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/example-6098.json" "file_sha256" "5c00836c23f8dab4689ed00b0cf5aba59fd496209e93effa15f734da9a1b8706"} {"question" "e-6098" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[-\\frac{y}{x}]}_{2}^{4}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(-\\frac{y}{4}-(-\\frac{y}{2}))\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}\\,\\text{d}y & ={[\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/example-6098.json" "file_sha256" "5c00836c23f8dab4689ed00b0cf5aba59fd496209e93effa15f734da9a1b8706"} {"question" "e-6099" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D = \\big\\{ (x,y) \\: : \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1 \\big\\}.$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A  = \\int_{0}^{1}  \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,  \\text{d}y \\, \\text{d}x$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A  = \\int_{0}^{2}  \\int_{0}^{1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\, \\text{d}y\\,  \\text{d}x$\n\n- $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A = \\int_{0}^{1}  \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,  \\text{d}x \\, \\text{d}y$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/example-6099.json" "file_sha256" "b7678c818036e4668afc9d84208be555e73bcf5caa84aac7f99c60b756a8dbe2"} {"question" "e-6099" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice that: \n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from ${\\color{blue}0}$ to ${\\color{blue}2}$, and\n\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from ${\\color{red}0}$ to ${\\color{red}1}.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A  \n= \\int_{\\color{blue}0}^{\\color{blue}{2}} \\left[ \\int_{\\color{red}0}^{\\color{red}1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}{\\color{red}y} \\right] \\text{d}{\\color{blue}x} .\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042681/example-6099.json" "file_sha256" "b7678c818036e4668afc9d84208be555e73bcf5caa84aac7f99c60b756a8dbe2"}] "usage" {"e-6099" [] "e-6097" [] "e-6098" []} "basis" 1726 "retractions" [[17592186128918 :question/problem "Evaluate the repeated integral $\\displaystyle \\int_{2}^{4} \\int_{0}^{2} \\dfrac{x^3}{y^2} \\, \\textrm{d}x \\, \\textrm{d}y$."] [17592186128918 :question/worked-solution "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{2}^{4}[∫_{0}^{2}\\frac{x^{3}}{y^{2}}dx]dy &= ∫_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{y^{2}}[\\frac{x^{4}}{4}]_{0}^{2}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{y^{2}}(\\frac{2^{4}}{4} - \\frac{0^{4}}{4})dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{2}^{4}\\frac{4}{y^{2}}dy \\\\\n&= 4∫_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{y^{2}}dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4∫_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{y^{2}}dy &= 4[- \\frac{1}{y}]_{2}^{4} \\\\\n&= 4(-\\frac{1}{4} - (-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\\n&= 4 \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\\n&= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186128919 :question/problem "Evaluate the double integral $\\displaystyle \\iint \\limits_{D} \\dfrac y{x^2} \\, \\textrm d A$, where\n$D=\\left\\{(x,y) \\:: \\:2 \\leq x \\leq 4,\\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 3\\right\\}$."] [17592186128919 :question/worked-solution "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)\\frac{y}{x^{2}}dA &= ∫_{0}^{3}[∫_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{x^{2}}dx]dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{3}[∫_{2}^{4}\\frac{y}{x^{2}}dx]dy &= ∫_{0}^{3}[- \\frac{y}{x}]_{2}^{4}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{3}(-\\frac{y}{4} - (-\\frac{y}{2}))dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{3}\\frac{y}{4}dy &= [\\frac{y^{2}}{8}]_{0}^{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{3^{2}}{8} - \\frac{0^{2}}{8} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9}{8}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186128920 :question/problem "Which of the following equalities are true given that\n$D = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\leq x \\leq 2, \\: 0 \\leq y \\leq 1 \\big\\}$.\n\n1. $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A = \\int_{0}^{1} \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\, \\text{d}y \\, \\text{d}x$\n2. $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}A = \\int_{0}^{2} \\int_{0}^{1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\, \\text{d}y\\, \\text{d}x$\n3. $\\displaystyle \\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A = \\int_{0}^{1} \\int_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\, \\text{d}x \\, \\text{d}y$"] [17592186128920 :question/worked-solution "We notice that:\n\n- the limits for the variable $x$ are from ${\\color{blue}0}$ to ${\\color{blue}2}$, and\n- the limits for the variable $y$ are from ${\\color{red}0}$ to ${\\color{red}1}$.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∬_(D)e^{\\sqrt{xy}}dA &= ∫_{0}^{1}[∫_{0}^{2}e^{\\sqrt{xy}}dx]dy\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the region of integration is rectangular, we can simply swap the order of integration. This gives\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_{D} e^{\\sqrt{xy}} \\,\\text{d}A = \\int_{\\color{blue}0}^{\\color{blue}{2}} \\left[ \\int_{\\color{red}0}^{\\color{red}1} e^{\\sqrt{xy}}\\,\\text{d}{\\color{red}y} \\right] \\text{d}{\\color{blue}x}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"."]] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
